.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL_FILE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OPENSSL_FILE ,
.Nm OPENSSL_LINE ,
.Nm OPENSSL_FUNC ,
.Nm OPENSSL_MSTR ,
.Nm OPENSSL_MSTR_HELPER
.Nd generic C programming utility macros
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/macros.h
.Fd #define OPENSSL_FILE /* typically: __FILE__ */
.Fd #define OPENSSL_LINE /* typically: __LINE__ */
.Fd #define OPENSSL_FUNC /* typically: __func__ */
.Fd #define OPENSSL_MSTR_HELPER(x) #x
.Fd #define OPENSSL_MSTR(x) OPENSSL_MSTR_HELPER(x)
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The macros
.Sy OPENSSL_FILE
and
.Sy OPENSSL_LINE
typically yield the current filename and line number during C
compilation.
When
.Sy OPENSSL_NO_FILENAMES
is defined they yield
.Sy \(dq"
and
.Sy 0 ,
respectively.
.Pp
The macro
.Sy OPENSSL_FUNC
attempts to yield the name of the C function currently being compiled,
as far as language and compiler versions allow.
Otherwise, it yields "(unknown function)".
.Pp
The macro
.Sy OPENSSL_MSTR
yields the expansion of the macro given as argument, which is useful for
concatenation with string constants.
The macro
.Sy OPENSSL_MSTR_HELPER
is an auxiliary macro for this purpose.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
see above
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crypto 7
.Sh HISTORY
.Sy OPENSSL_FUNC ,
.Sy OPENSSL_MSTR ,
and
.Sy OPENSSL_MSTR_HELPER
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
